) AXAuthorization as a closed object (exactly lease_id:UUIDv4, lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991], holder_host_id:UUIDv7 and the remaining members exactly as the pinned section lists them, no extra and no missing member, unknown member refused), parsed through the landed canonicaljson closed-shape discipline, with the epoch bound witnessed at 1, 9007199254740991 and both adjacent out-of-range values; today `Transition.Authorization` is only a string, so every operation's authorization requirement must become a checked object.\n4|(2) The closed RetryDisposition enum — exactly replay_same, status_first, new_authorization, required_operator_action — carried by every result, plus the request/result identity contract: every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and idempotency IDs, the exact backend ID/version/generation, a deadline and an expiring AX authorization with the winning lease ID/epoch; every result repeats those identities and adds before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs and exactly one retry disposition.\n5|(3) The state-entry rules, each one driven and each one mutated: `creating` is entered only by `create`, only after its durable idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect; an error BEFORE a side effect restores the source state; an error AFTER an effect whose result cannot be proven moves the local observation to `unavailable` with `status_first` and MUST NOT claim `absent`; no operation other than `quiesce-input` enters `quiescing`; no backend operation enters `stale_fenced` — only AX fencing observation does (drive that from the landed internal/fencing projection, do not invent a second fencing model); authorization AND generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect (not once at entry); a deadline cancels waiting but never a committed effect.\n6|(4) Generation-safe evidence: `backend_generation` is the canonical string[1..256] bound in every containing contract — reject lengths 0 and 25