{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":266,"recorded_at":1780531400000527,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b234-03d7-74a2-a0b1-fef009cf208e"},"task_id":"01a0b234-03d7-74a2-a0b1-fef009cf208e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b234-03d7-74a2-a0b1-fef009cf208e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"R=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/base-refresh/replay-563536699/worktree; git -C $R diff --stat; echo ===CONFLICT-MARKERS===; grep -n '^<<<<<<<\\\\|^=======\\\\|^>>>>>>>' $R/LOGBOOK.md | head; echo ===HEAD-60===; head -n 60 $R/LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect LOGBOOK conflict in replay worktree\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \" LOGBOOK.md | Unmerged\\n LOGBOOK.md | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)\\n===CONFLICT-MARKERS===\\n8:<<<<<<< HEAD\\n16:=======\\n33:>>>>>>> e6fe5c5 (TASK-260830-1geqhj: TASK-260830-1geqhj: implement-ax-pane-enforcement-wrapper)\\n===HEAD-60===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n<<<<<<< HEAD\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n- REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n- TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\\n- P3 GAPS (all closed with a failing-without-it test): opaque-body object gate over `health.get` (`[]`/`null`/`\\\"x\\\"`/`42`/duplicate-member → ErrFrame) + `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bodies with an I-JSON object oracle (the naive `&& op !=` plant is vacuous — the stale `err` still propagates — so the committed probe restructures the gate); changed-body retry after a committed effect → literal `idempotency_mismatch` with a single retained journal (one-off J1 overlay kills the new test, staging still passes); body-fuzzer oracle bound stated explicitly (member-name + object + round-trip only; bounds/vocabularies owned by the unit suite) + hello-body-extra seed in `FuzzUnknownFields`; exact 8388608-admit/8388609-refuse encode edge; `ErrVersionMismatch` class pinned in the error-schema lanes; literal `[2 3 4]`/`[5]` offer sets in the N2 rows; nonce-alphabet plant widened to the full unpadded standard-base64 class (two-arm `RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\\n- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n=======\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev4 — ax pane rework: fold-only newest, resumed-checkpoint closure, replay signal\\n- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev3 (1 P1 class at two sites, 1 P2, 8 P3): the strict lease/fold equality is deleted — the fold is the sole newest authority and a successor lease's checkpoint is the handoff base at takeover time that never moves, so the only asserted fact is the implication \\\"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\\\" at one site directly after fencing (launch and restore alike, parked `restore_policy` on a null fold); `Run` derives the profile closure from the checkpoint actually resumed (required checkpoint, else fold newest, else session head), never `Winner.Checkpoint`; `Supersede` reports the commit-race replay and `Run` flips the post-window loser to `reattach`; the window never closes on the lease record, an unfoldable chain fails the run, and the identity record binds its own `session_id`.\\n- F1: an immutable handoff base can only ever imply, never equal, a moving newest — the equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint, and relaxing it alone turned the park into a wrong-profile launch, so both sites landed together with the post-takeover lifecycle positive (restore launches with C1's closure) and the wrong-profile plants in both directions through `Run`.\\n- F2: a store-level replay without a signal is a lie at the call site — `Supersede` replayed the winner's receipt but `Run` reported `launch` with a child it did not create; the `(Binding, bool, error)` signal mirrors `Bind`'s `reattached` and flips the outcome, pinned through `Run` with the `AfterStage` hook.\\n- F3: per-object classification cannot be derived from an aggregate error — `Reconcile` liveness shares the generic mismatch code and carries no per-row identity, so the `realmRowUsable` copy is a stated classification-only bound, fail-closed both directions; likewise the handoff-base-to-published binding is the takeover leaf's stated obligation.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 52 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 53/53 with control), including the null-fold conditional row, the closure-source row (a mutant reading `Winner.Checkpoint` again dies), the replay-keeps-launch row, the lease-closes-window row, and the fold-error-laundered row. AC 43/43 re-derived by counting with every named test verified present; the four rev3-unfaithful rows now pin the post-takeover launch positives.\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev3 — ax pane rework: fold newest, per-pair receipts, credential conditional\\n- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev2 (1 P1 class, 2 P2, 8 P3): the bootstrap window, checkpoint admission, and journal source binding now read the chain fold's newest checkpoint (`sessstate.Reduce` → `Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest.ID`) instead of the lease record's checkpoint, which is null for every epoch-1 owner; a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold; superseded pairs keep per-operation receipts (`receipts/<op>.json`, no-replace per pair) with the first binding as the in-window anchor; `Run` fails when a checkpoint-carrying winner has no checkpoint store bound; the §4.C credential conditional applies to every caller with `Smoke.Required`, the realm cross-bind accepts any binding object, and dead (expired/pre-reboot) realm evidence refuses the typed `capability_unavailable`.\\n- F1: lease records are immutable content-addressed blobs — `CreateLease` mints epoch-1 with a null checkpoint and only a takeover mints a checkpoint-carrying successor — so \\\"the winning lease's checkpoint\\\" can never be the newest-checkpoint authority; the ordinary same-host story (stopped with C on epoch 1) is the test that catches the confusion at all three gates (window/admission/journal) at both `Decide` and `Run`.\\n- F2: per-pair receipts keep the §4.1 replay contract (\\\"identical retry replays it\\\", keyed `session_id + \\\"/\\\" + bootstrap_operation_id`) while the first-binding anchor keeps the in-window mutual exclusion the link race proved; `SessionBound` scans anchor-or-receipts so a crash between installs cannot reopen the window.\\n- F3: `Reconcile` fails before the realm arm runs, so dead realm evidence needs a refusal mapping, not a wider gate: the mapping fires only when the caller needs the realm row, submitted a realm row, and none is usable — a usable row plus an unrelated backend fault keeps the backend class.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 47 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 48/48 with control), including one narrowing mutant per P1-1 conditional (window-fold, null-fold ×2, newest, agreement ×2) and the RV7 losing-epoch row the rev2 suite survived. AC 43/43 re-derived by counting (rev2's \\\"41 of 41\\\" restated a 43-row denominator; the reviewer measured 39/43).\\n- REVERSAL (P1-1, stated explicitly): this entry's \\\"a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold\\\" is FALSE as of rev4 — a successor lease's `checkpoint_id` is the handoff base at takeover time and never moves, while every checkpoint the successor owner publishes afterwards lands on the chain, so the strict equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint and parked every session that was ever taken over. The fold is the sole newest authority; the only asserted fact is the implication \\\"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\\\" (one site, directly after fencing), and the profile closure comes from the checkpoint actually resumed, never `Winner.Checkpoint`.\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n>>>>>>> e6fe5c5 (TASK-260830-1geqhj: TASK-260830-1geqhj: implement-ax-pane-enforcement-wrapper)\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev2 — ax pane rework: authority, window, closure, realm\\n- REWORKED on `888ae3d` after review-verdict-rev1 (18 findings): event authority through `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` with local-hold-only emission and the §5.7 fold gate (`sessstate.Reduce`); realm authorization through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to host binding/build/generation (bare boolean removed); bootstrap window closed by the winner's `HasCheckpoint` with atomic `Supersede`; checkpoint admission bound to the winning lease and session; profile from the checkpoint closure (`DeriveForHeads`); journal source bound to the lease checkpoint; non-interactive `headless_creation` conditional; remote non-interactive parks per §4.2 step 5.\\n- F1: a park decision's stale/unverified presented token never authors — `Emit` presents the winning tuple itself, so verified local-winner parks (stale, material, checkpoint) emit while remote/unverified/ambiguous/handoff parks refuse; `Run` pre-checks local hold + foldability and parks without evidence rather than manufacturing a §5.2 collision.\\n- REVERSAL (P3-8, stated explicitly): rev1 F1's \\\"both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`\\\" is FALSE as of rev2 — `attach_remote`, `takeover_offer`, and every remote park author no chain event, because the local wrapper cannot append under another host's lease (§5.2: the winning owner serializes state-changing events); the decision itself is the parked evidence.\\n- F2: the bootstrap window is the winner's `HasCheckpoint`, not a clock: in-window changed ops refuse `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes, post-window new ops supersede via staged rename; the `binding-*.tmp` sweep is age-gated (1 min) so a concurrent live stage is never deleted.\\n- F3: resume profile is the checkpoint closure, not the head: `Run` loads the winner's heads even when the checkpoint is not otherwise required, so a head-only or losing-lease `profile.changed` never drives launch (§2.4, §13.10).\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 35 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with control); reviewer's RM1/RM2/RM4 survivors now killed by `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`, `TestDecideRemoteOwnerPrecedesMaterialization`, `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`. AC 41/41 re-derived with the six previously unfaithful rows re-pinned.\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/axpane` — the pure `Decide` core (`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked|refused`), the `Run` orchestration over real stores, the durable bootstrap `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` binding store, §5.2 event authorship, and the §7.A descriptor builder. Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`, `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`, `terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented. First leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n- F1: `fencing` launch entries refuse — not park — foreign sessions, malformed tokens, and lapsed grants, so the wrapper's `refused(lease_conflict)` rows for foreign/expired inputs compose directly; only remote/ambiguous/unverified/absent/stale ownership parks. Remote parks resolve locally to `attach_remote` (interactive + attach admitted) or `takeover_offer`, and both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`.\\n- F2: the tuple gate must precede profile mapping in arm order: `ResolveMapping` re-checks the tuple internally, so mapping-first would wear tuple refusals as `profile_mapping_unavailable`. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call stays as fail-fast ordering; weakening it alone is unobservable (defense in depth, stated in TRACEABILITY.md).\\n- F3: `terminalbackend.Reconcile` maps generation drift to the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation` (not the generic mismatch), and `create` is conferred by both `durable_disconnect` and `headless_creation` — the unproven vector must deny both. `sessckpt.Get` re-attests through `sessrepo` on every read, so checkpoint admission composes through the read path.\\n- F4: `Bind` is linearizable on the commit race via link-EEXIST re-read (same operation reattaches to the winner, changed operation refuses); the `AfterStage` hook plays the concurrent winner deterministically in tests. The store stamps `created_at` itself — scalar timestamps require ≥3 fractional digits, so `time.RFC3339Nano` (which omits trailing zeros) is not a valid stamp.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 24 narrowing mutants, all KILLED by named tests through `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, plus the applied harmless SURVIVED control (25/25 rows match; per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in the outcome tar). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n- AC: 41 of 41 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260917-10k118: reconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk 7efe385 (STORY-260916-3uqbwq unlandable, accepted CRs frozen)\\n- METHOD: true pin delta is `git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4` (10 files) — the exported 238-file patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so it was used as transport only; rev3 candidate bytes applied (15 modified + 3 new) with the 5 trunk-merged files copied verbatim after diff-review (no trunk test lost, `task-board.config.json` untouched). All 19 machine-applied files `cmp`-identical to the rev3 bytes; ownership sha256 `2548870d…8a5070`, projection digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6` recomputed two independent ways.\\n- RE-VERIFIED (this session, fresh clone + production helpers): tag `d4abe46f…795b3` Good, peeled `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes sha256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table (1 known order normalization); 65/65 bindings + 132/132 cases carried with 3 reviewed additions each; all 49 discharged clauses re-measured (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392, excerpts verbatim); rev3 prose says \\\"48 carried clause lines\\\" in two places — measured 49, matching the 49/569 numerator; artifact is right, prose miscounted.\\n- FINDING F1: the reviewed v0.7.0 source normative-section group keeps production `VerifyV060` while its cases moved to the v0.7.0 pair; the v0.5.0→v0.6.0 precedent moved `Verify`→`VerifyV060`, so the pattern says `VerifyV070`. Green because the gate checks declaration existence only. Reviewed bytes are not rewritten in a reconstruction; the new re-derivation test pins the carried reference literally with the rationale.\\n- NEW TESTS (this Story's scope): `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (carry completeness, clause re-measurement via production inventory+quote, no self-minted claims) and `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` (fenced line byte-equal to tool output, 8 headline prose figures re-derived). Narrowing mutants per test + token-preserving README plant with full behavioral suites; harmless controls SURVIVED. Full 27-command suite green on the exact tree.\\n- FIGURES: contracts=64, acceptance cases=135, bindings=68, clauses 49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 17759,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4440,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
