{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c58d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":289,"recorded_at":1780531400000573,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"call_id":"call_01a0b234206172429ae24e1d823c4333","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-10-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git show c3aae73:LOGBOOK.md > /tmp/logbook_trunk.md; git show e6fe5c5:LOGBOOK.md > /tmp/logbook_ckpt.md; wc -l /tmp/logbook_trunk.md /tmp/logbook_ckpt.md; echo ===TRUNK-HEAD-30===; head -n 30 /tmp/logbook_trunk.md; echo ===CKPT-HEAD-40===; head -n 40 /tmp/logbook_ckpt.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Extract both LOGBOOK versions for resolution\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"    2426 /tmp/logbook_trunk.md\\n    2444 /tmp/logbook_ckpt.md\\n    4870 total\\n===TRUNK-HEAD-30===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n- REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n- TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\\n- P3 GAPS (all closed with a failing-without-it test): opaque-body object gate over `health.get` (`[]`/`null`/`\\\"x\\\"`/`42`/duplicate-member → ErrFrame) + `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bodies with an I-JSON object oracle (the naive `&& op !=` plant is vacuous — the stale `err` still propagates — so the committed probe restructures the gate); changed-body retry after a committed effect → literal `idempotency_mismatch` with a single retained journal (one-off J1 overlay kills the new test, staging still passes); body-fuzzer oracle bound stated explicitly (member-name + object + round-trip only; bounds/vocabularies owned by the unit suite) + hello-body-extra seed in `FuzzUnknownFields`; exact 8388608-admit/8388609-refuse encode edge; `ErrVersionMismatch` class pinned in the error-schema lanes; literal `[2 3 4]`/`[5]` offer sets in the N2 rows; nonce-alphabet plant widened to the full unpadded standard-base64 class (two-arm `RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\\n- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260917-10k118: reconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk 7efe385 (STORY-260916-3uqbwq unlandable, accepted CRs frozen)\\n- METHOD: true pin delta is `git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4` (10 files) — the exported 238-file patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so it was used as transport only; rev3 candidate bytes applied (15 modified + 3 new) with the 5 trunk-merged files copied verbatim after diff-review (no trunk test lost, `task-board.config.json` untouched). All 19 machine-applied files `cmp`-identical to the rev3 bytes; ownership sha256 `2548870d…8a5070`, projection digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6` recomputed two independent ways.\\n- RE-VERIFIED (this session, fresh clone + production helpers): tag `d4abe46f…795b3` Good, peeled `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes sha256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table (1 known order normalization); 65/65 bindings + 132/132 cases carried with 3 reviewed additions each; all 49 discharged clauses re-measured (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392, excerpts verbatim); rev3 prose says \\\"48 carried clause lines\\\" in two places — measured 49, matching the 49/569 numerator; artifact is right, prose miscounted.\\n- FINDING F1: the reviewed v0.7.0 source normative-section group keeps production `VerifyV060` while its cases moved to the v0.7.0 pair; the v0.5.0→v0.6.0 precedent moved `Verify`→`VerifyV060`, so the pattern says `VerifyV070`. Green because the gate checks declaration existence only. Reviewed bytes are not rewritten in a reconstruction; the new re-derivation test pins the carried reference literally with the rationale.\\n- NEW TESTS (this Story's scope): `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (carry completeness, clause re-measurement via production inventory+quote, no self-minted claims) and `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` (fenced line byte-equal to tool output, 8 headline prose figures re-derived). Narrowing mutants per test + token-preserving README plant with full behavioral suites; harmless controls SURVIVED. Full 27-command suite green on the exact tree.\\n- FIGURES: contracts=64, acceptance cases=135, bindings=68, clauses 49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim.\\n- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260916-n9r71p: bound v0.7.0 launch-plan catalog row and curator story owners\\n- AUTHORITY: catalogue generation, Current, CI roots and traceability consume the adopted v0.7.0 lock/document/inventory; four release projections preserve V060/V050/V043 history. Metadata digest `c4094101…50274a35`; ownership digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6`. Localstore stays on explicit CurrentV050. Validation command 22 is the release-ag