{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c73b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":504,"recorded_at":1780531400001003,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b235-c0ba-7d22-a002-16e2d38420d6"},"task_id":"01a0b235-c0ba-7d22-a002-16e2d38420d6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b235-c0ba-7d22-a002-16e2d38420d6","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-19-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 20 LOGBOOK.md; echo ===HEAD-VERSION===; git show HEAD:LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20; echo ===README-ANCHOR-HEAD===; git show HEAD:README.md | grep -n -e 'Ownership reducer properties' -e 'axpane/TRACEABILITY' | head; echo ===README-ANCHOR-WT===; grep -n -e 'Ownership reducer properties' -e 'terminstance' README.md | head\",\n  \"description\": \"Compare working tree vs new HEAD for candidate paths\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/terminstance` — the §4.C execution layer over the landed `terminalbackend` core: closed `AXAuthorization` (UUIDv4 lease, uint53 epoch bound, UUIDv7 holder, kind, timestamps, digest) through the `environ` closed-shape discipline, closed `RetryDisposition`/`ProviderProofKind` enums, the `MutationContext`/`MutationResult` identity contract with exact per-row idempotency material, and the `Engine` (durable receipt before first effect, per-effect auth+generation rechecks, source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` post-commit, deadline cancels waiting never committed effects). `stale_fenced` enters only through `fencing` park vocabulary; status is receipt/effect-free and unknown is never absent. Second leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n- F1: quiesce-input and request-stop carry no conditional beyond conferral — their spec capabilities are their sole conferring registry rows — so the landed `CheckOperation` decides those rows alone and a second arm restating it would be dead code; the engine's conditional covers only create-headless, wait-safe-plus-provider-iff, and status-provider, where the spec demands more than conferral.\\n- F2: the receipt's no-replace commit needs a separate completion file, because the result is unknown at bind time and updating the receipt in place would break no-replace; pending-without-done is therefore the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` with `status_first` instead of replaying or inventing absence.\\n- F3: the epoch high edge cannot be weakened past `environ`'s own uint53 ceiling (same value, equivalent mutant), so that harness row tightens instead and proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it; the min edge, the delegate's ceiling, and the tightening row triangulate the bound.\\n- F4: closed P3-6 from the predecessor review (the `Decision.Descriptor` doc now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on reattach); P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader in this package); P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to the final leaf with the recovery/events reasons.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 51 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 53/53 with the harmless SURVIVED control), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n- AC: 72 of 72 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`, every named test verified present via `go test -list`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-SIGKILL pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n- F5 (finding, pre-existing): `TestSmokeThroughRealProviderProcess` (`internal/resumesmoke`, `probe=fail`) fails identically on the committed base HEAD without this leaf's changes and has no dependency edge to either leaf (`go list -deps` clean; base packages untouched by both leaves), so commands 4–6 report exit 1 with that single named cause while all 38 other packages — including `terminstance`, `axpane`, `terminalbackend` — are green in the full, race, and coverage runs alike.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev4 — ax pane rework: fold-only newest, resumed-checkpoint closure, replay signal\\n- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev3 (1 P1 class at two sites, 1 P2, 8 P3): the strict lease/fold equality is deleted — the fold is the sole newest authority and a successor lease's checkpoint is the handoff base at takeover time that never moves, so the only asserted fact is the implication \\\"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\\\" at one site directly after fencing (launch and restore alike, parked `restore_policy` on a null fold); `Run` derives the profile closure from the checkpoint actually resumed (required checkpoint, else fold newest, else session head), never `Winner.Checkpoint`; `Supersede` reports the commit-race replay and `Run` flips the post-window loser to `reattach`; the window never closes on the lease record, an unfoldable chain fails the run, and the identity record binds its own `session_id`.\\n- F1: an immutable handoff base can only ever imply, never equal, a moving newest — the equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint, and relaxing it alone turned the park into a wrong-profile launch, so both sites landed together with the post-takeover lifecycle positive (restore launches with C1's closure) and the wrong-profile plants in both directions through `Run`.\\n===HEAD-VERSION===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n- REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n- TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\\n- P3 GAPS (all closed with a failing-without-it test): opaque-body object gate over `health.get` (`[]`/`null`/`\\\"x\\\"`/`42`/duplicate-member → ErrFrame) + `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bodies with an I-JSON object oracle (the naive `&& op !=` plant is vacuous — the stale `err` still propagates — so the committed probe restructures the gate); changed-body retry after a committed effect → literal `idempotency_mismatch` with a single retained journal (one-off J1 overlay kills the new test, staging still passes); body-fuzzer oracle bound stated explicitly (member-name + object + round-trip only; bounds/vocabularies owned by the unit suite) + hello-body-extra seed in `FuzzUnknownFields`; exact 8388608-admit/8388609-refuse encode edge; `ErrVersionMismatch` class pinned in the error-schema lanes; literal `[2 3 4]`/`[5]` offer sets in the N2 rows; nonce-alphabet plant widened to the full unpadded standard-base64 class (two-arm `RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\\n- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev4 — ax pane rework: fold-only newest, resumed-checkpoint closure, replay signal\\n- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev3 (1 P1 class at two sites, 1 P2, 8 P3): the strict lease/fold equality is deleted — the fold is the sole newest authority and a successor lease's checkpoint is the handoff base at takeover time that never moves, so the only asserted fact is the implication \\\"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\\\" at one site directly after fencing (launch and restore alike, parked `restore_policy` on a null fold); `Run` derives the profile closure from the checkpoint actually resumed (required checkpoint, else fold newest, else session head), never `Winner.Checkpoint`; `Supersede` reports the commit-race replay and `Run` flips the post-window loser to `reattach`; the window never closes on the lease record, an unfoldable chain fails the run, and the identity record binds its own `session_id`.\\n- F1: an immutable handoff base can only ever imply, never equal, a moving newest — the equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint, and relaxing it alone turned the park into a wrong-profile launch, so both sites landed together with the post-takeover lifecycle positive (restore launches with C1's closure) and the wrong-profile plants in both directions through `Run`.\\n- F2: a store-level replay without a signal is a lie at the call site — `Supersede` replayed the winner's receipt but `Run` reported `launch` with a child it did not create; the `(Binding, bool, error)` signal mirrors `Bind`'s `reattached` and flips the outcome, pinned through `Run` with the `AfterStage` hook.\\n- F3: per-object classification cannot be derived from an aggregate error — `Reconcile` liveness shares the generic mismatch code and carries no per-row identity, so the `realmRowUsable` copy is a stated classification-only bound, fail-closed both directions; likewise the handoff-base-to-published binding is the takeover leaf's stated obligation.\\n===README-ANCHOR-HEAD===\\n2212:[the task evidence map](internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n2215:## Ownership reducer properties\\n===README-ANCHOR-WT===\\n2214:## Terminal Instance lifecycle execution (`terminstance` engine)\\n2216:[`internal/terminstance`](internal/terminstance) executes the Terminal\\n2241:go test ./internal/terminstance -count=1\\n2242:go test ./internal/terminstance -cover -count=1\\n2249:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/terminstance/mutant_harness.py\\n2259:[the task evidence map](internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n2261:## Ownership reducer properties\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 11600,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2900,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
