he post-takeover lifecycle positive (restore launches with C1's closure) and the wrong-profile plants in both directions through `Run`.\\n===HEAD-VERSION===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n- REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n- TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally