{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca23","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":876,"recorded_at":1780531400001747,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"call_id":"call_01a0b236c93f70debd8d21c2ed1a8239","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-kkh1an/TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-kkh1an — producer results\n2|\n3|Task: implement the Terminal Instance lifecycle state machine (second\n4|leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe, EPIC M1). Trunk: `2fc6d50`\n5|(`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, headings byte-identical to v0.6.0\n6|in scope); `origin/main` verified equal to the candidate base at\n7|handoff time (see validation below), so no refresh was needed.\n8|Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot.\n9|\n10|## What was built\n11|\n12|`internal/terminstance` (new package) executes the §4.C lifecycle\n13|contract over the landed `internal/terminalbackend` core, per the\n14|producer scope items (1)-(5):\n15|\n16|- (1) `AXAuthorization` as a closed 7-member object\n17|  (`ParseAXAuthorization`), parsed through the landed `environ`\n18|  closed-shape discipline with the epoch bound witnessed at 1,\n19|  9007199254740991 and both adjacent out-of-range values; every\n20|  engine operation's authorization requirement is a checked object\n21|  (`CheckAuthorization`: kind, expiry, lease identity, lease epoch).\n22|- (2) The closed `RetryDisposition` enum (4 members) carried by every\n23|  result, plus the request/result identity contract\n24|  (`MutationContext`/`MutationResult`, `CheckResult` repetition arms,\n25|  per-row idempotency material through landed `IdempotencyKey`).\n26|- (3) The state-entry rules in `Engine`: receipt before first effect,\n27|  source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` on\n28|  unprovable post-commit errors (never `absent`), `creating` only via\n29|  `create`, `quiescing` only via `quiesce-input`, `stale_fenced` only\n30|  via `ObserveFencing` (landed `fencing` park vocabulary), per-effect\n31|  auth+generation rechecks, deadline cancels waiting never committed\n32|  effects.\n33|- (4) The canonical `backend_generation` string[1..256] bound in\n34|  every owned surface (0/257 refuse, 256 admits, characters not\n35|  bytes), with staleness refusing the landed\n36|  `terminal_backend_stale_generation` class; bound verdicts agree\n37|  with landed `GenerationDigest` on the boundary corpus.\n38|- (5) The status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary and request-stop\n39|  rows (sources, targets, effects, key material, evidence\n40|  capabilities, exact refusal sets with outside-set rejection via\n41|  landed `CheckErrorAllowed`), plus the create receipt rule.\n42|\n43|Which existing type or gate each addition extends is tabulated in\n44|`internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md` (Landed extensions); no\n45|second state machine, enum, fencing model, or JSON discipline was\n46|forked.\n47|\n48|## AC coverage: 72 of 72 rows driven\n49|\n50|Measured, not restated: 72 data rows counted in\n51|`internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`, every named test verified\n52|present via `go test -list` (69 names, zero missing; see\n53|`ratio-check.log`), and the full package suite green\n54|(`terminstance-test-v.log`: 157 `--- PASS`, 0 `--- FAIL`).\n55|Production call sites are named per row in the matrix.\n56|\n57|## Negative and mutant evidence\n58|\n59|- `mutant_harness.py`: 53/53 rows match on two full passes — 51\n60|  narrowing KILLED + 1 tightening edge KILLED + the SURVIVED\n61|  control. The tightening row (`N-auth-epoch-high`) is documented:\n62|  weakening past `MaxLeaseEpoch` is equivalent because `environ`\n63|  refuses 2^53 at the number layer, so the row proves the edge is\n64|  exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it. Per-plant raw logs with\n65|  subprocess exits in `mutants/pass1/` and `mutants/pass2/`\n66|  (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); production blobs\n67|  verified byte-identical before/after (`blob-oids-*.txt`).\n68|- Crash/idempotency: no-replace link commits on receipt and\n69|  completion paths, `AfterCommit` hook seam, real-SIGKILL test\n70|  (`TestExecuteCrashChildSelfTerminates`); pending-without-done\n71|  refuses uncertain and recovers through status, never absent.\n72|- No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects\n73|  source text.\n74|\n75|## Predecessor P3 advisories\n76|\n77|- P3-6 closed: `Decision.Descriptor` doc in `internal/axpane/decide.go`\n78|  now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on\n79|  reattach (comment-only; axpane suite re-run green).\n80|- P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds in this leaf's\n81|  TRACEABILITY (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader here).\n82|- P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to TASK-260830-2056mm with recovery/events\n83|  reasons (see TRACEABILITY).\n84|\n85|## Validation suite (configured commands, in order)\n86|\n87|Every command below is quoted verbatim from\n88|`task-board.config.json`\n89|`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (27 commands) and\n90|was executed once against the exact candidate tree; logs in `cmd/`.\n91|\n92|| # | Command | Exit |\n93|| --- | --- | --- |\n94|| 1 | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\"` | 0 |\n95|| 2 | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n96|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n97|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 1 — solely the pre-existing resumesmoke failure (38 packages ok) |\n98|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | 1 — solely the pre-existing resumesmoke failure (38 packages ok) |\n99|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 1 — solely the pre-existing resumesmoke failure (terminstance 82.3%) |\n100|| 7–12 | rpcwire/scalar/canonicaljson fuzz ×6 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×6 |\n101|| 13–20 | secconftest fuzz ×8 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×8 |\n102|| 21 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (contracts=64, cases=135, clauses 49/569 — trunk figures unchanged) |\n103|| 22 | `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | 0, tree unmodified |\n104|| 23 | `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n105|| 24 | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n106|| 25 | `git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c 'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'` | 0 |\n107|| 26 | `task-board validate` | 0 (184 pre-existing MISSING_ACTIVITY issues on unrelated elements; zero name this task or story) |\n108|| 27 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n109|\n110|Full logs in `cmd/` inside\n111|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`. The `.go` tree was\n112|verified byte-identical before and after the race gate\n113|(`go-sha-before-race.txt`), so the race ran against the exact\n114|candidate.\n115|\n116|## Pre-existing failure (finding, not a gate of this leaf)\n117|\n118|`TestSmokeThroughRealProviderProcess` (`internal/resumesmoke`,\n119|`probe=fail`) fails identically on the committed base HEAD without\n120|this leaf's changes (proven in a detached base worktree, since\n121|removed) and has no dependency edge to this leaf (`go list -deps`\n122|shows neither `terminstance` nor `axpane`); the base packages it\n123|covers are untouched by both story leaves (`git diff 2fc6d50\n124|e6fe5c5` touches only `internal/axpane`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`).\n125|`terminstance`, `axpane` and `terminalbackend` are green in the\n126|full, race, and coverage runs alike. Failing gates stay failing:\n127|commands 4–6 are reported exit 1 with the single named cause.\n128|\n129|## Files changed\n130|\n131|- `internal/terminstance/` (new package, untracked):\n132|  `doc.go`, `errors.go`, `auth.go`, `disposition.go`, `proof.go`,\n133|  `context.go`, `status.go`, `bodies.go`, `result.go`, `store.go`,\n134|  `fencing.go`, `execute.go`, `mutant_harness.py`,\n135|  `TRACEABILITY.md`, plus 13 test files.\n136|- `internal/axpane/decide.go`: P3-6 doc sentence (comment-only).\n137|- `README.md`: package section (additive).\n138|- `LOGBOOK.md`: leaf entry (additive, newest-first).\n139|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract.\n140|\n141|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n142|\n143|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added.\n144|Binding-object parsing, CLI Result 4, attach/restore/terminate-stale\n145|operations, full create body, credential conditionals, and terminal\n146|events are stated bounds (see TRACEABILITY.md). The per-code\n147|disposition mapping is the leaf's contract where the spec pins the\n148|vocabulary but not the mapping.\n149|\n150|## Handoff\n151|\n152|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n153|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n154|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md`,\n155|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_conformance-matrix.md`,\n156|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
