{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca4f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":898,"recorded_at":1780531400001791,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"call_id":"call_01a0b236d5f277c6924e261e6b6f6d7b","text":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# internal/terminstance — TRACEABILITY\n2|\n3|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §4.B (generation bound),\n4|§4.C (lifecycle and operations), §4.D (capability conditionals), §5.2\n5|(status/unknown discipline), §7.A (descriptor generation binding, cited\n6|landed), §13.1 (durable terminal entry before provider launch). Every\n7|row names the production entry and the committed test that drives it;\n8|every expectation asserts the literal specification token at the entry.\n9|Coverage: **72 of 72 AC rows driven** (counted below; verified by\n10|`go test ./internal/terminstance/ -count=1 -v`).\n11|\n12|## Landed extensions\n13|\n14|Every addition extends a landed type or gate; nothing is forked:\n15|\n16|| Addition | Extends |\n17|| --- | --- |\n18|| `ParseAXAuthorization`, `CheckAuthorization` | `terminalbackend.ParseAttachAuthorization` twin (shape discipline, strict expiry, binding checks); frame and member grammars delegated to `environ`/`scalar` |\n19|| `ParseRetryDisposition`, `DispositionFor` | New leaf contract over the landed row-code vocabulary (`terminalbackend` code consts aliased, never retyped) |\n20|| `ParseProviderProofKind`, `RequiresProviderObservation` | New leaf contract over the §4.C proof vocabulary |\n21|| `ParseMutationContext`, `CheckMutationContext`, `KeySegments` | `terminalbackend.IdempotencyKey` shapes, `ParseID`, `CheckVersionTuple`, `GenerationDigest` |\n22|| `ParseOperationBody`, `ParseStatusBody` | `environ.DecodeStrictObject` closed-shape discipline |\n23|| `Result`, `CheckResult` | `terminalbackend` state/effect vocabularies, `scalar` digests |\n24|| `Engine.ExecuteMutating`, `ExecuteStatus` | `terminalbackend.CheckTransition`, `CheckErrorAllowed`, `CheckOperation`, `CheckStatusResult` |\n25|| `ReceiptStore` | `terminalbackend.Receipt`/`Ledger`/`ImportLedger` triple and line encoding (byte-agreed, crash-durable) |\n26|| `ObserveFencing` | `fencing.Authorize` + `ParkDetails` (stale verdict only; no local tuple comparison) |\n27|| Engine error codes | `terminalbackend` code consts aliased; the four literals the landed core spells only inside its allowed-error table (`terminal_backend_timeout`, `terminal_backend_process_failed`, `quiesce_timeout`, `stop_timeout`) pinned admitted by `TestRowCodesAreAdmittedByCheckErrorAllowed` |\n28|\n29|## AC rows\n30|\n31|### AXAuthorization (item 1) — `ParseAXAuthorization`, `CheckAuthorization`\n32|\n33|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n34|| --- | --- | --- |\n35|| 1 | Closed 7-member object admitted, every member literal | `TestParseAXAuthorizationAdmitsClosedFixture` |\n36|| 2 | lease_id is UUIDv4 (v7, garbage, number refuse) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n37|| 3 | lease_epoch 1 admitted | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n38|| 4 | lease_epoch 9007199254740991 admitted | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n39|| 5 | lease_epoch 0 refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n40|| 6 | lease_epoch 9007199254740992 refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n41|| 7 | Epoch AX number model (fraction, exponent, sign, string, bool, null, huge refuse) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochNumberModel` |\n42|| 8 | holder_host_id is UUIDv7 | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n43|| 9 | authorization_kind closed create/control/force_stale/restore | `TestParseAXAuthorizationKindClosed` |\n44|| 10 | Strict expiry (equal and inverted refuse unauthorized) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationStrictExpiry` |\n45|| 11 | authorization_evidence_id is a digest | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n46|| 12 | Unknown member refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n47|| 13 | Missing member refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n48|| 14 | Frame violations (non-object, trailing, duplicate, surrogate, non-UTF8) refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n49|| 15 | Kind binding (control presented as create refuses) | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/kind_mismatch` |\n50|| 16 | Expiry at and past the edge refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/expired`, `/expiry_edge_refuses` |\n51|| 17 | Lease identity drift refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_identity_drift` |\n52|| 18 | Lease epoch drift refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_epoch_drift` |\n53|\n54|### Closed enums (item 2) — `ParseRetryDisposition`, `ParseProviderProofKind`, `ParseAuthorizationKind`, `DispositionFor`\n55|\n56|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n57|| --- | --- | --- |\n58|| 19 | RetryDisposition closed replay_same/status_first/new_authorization/required_operator_action | `TestParseRetryDispositionClosed`, `TestClosedEnumsAreExactlyPinned` |\n59|| 20 | Per-code disposition mapping (26 literal rows) | `TestDispositionForMapping` |\n60|| 21 | ProviderProofKind closed provider_quiescence/provider_process_exit/ax_checkpoint_boundary | `TestParseProviderProofKindClosed`, `TestClosedEnumsAreExactlyPinned` |\n61|| 22 | Provider classification (2 provider kinds, AX boundary not) | `TestRequiresProviderObservation` |\n62|| 23 | AuthorizationKind closed create/control/force_stale/restore | `TestParseAuthorizationKindClosed`, `TestClosedEnumsAreExactlyPinned` |\n63|\n64|### Request identity (item 2) — `ParseMutationContext`, `CheckMutationContext`, `KeySegments`\n65|\n66|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n67|| --- | --- | --- |\n68|| 24 | Closed 10-member context admitted, every member literal | `TestParseMutationContextAdmitsClosedFixture` |\n69|| 25 | Context member grammars (UUIDs, backend ID, versions, key, deadline, nested auth) | `TestParseMutationContextMemberRefusals` |\n70|| 26 | Generation 0/257 refuse stale class, 256 and multibyte-256 admit | `TestParseMutationContextMemberRefusals`, `TestParseMutationContextGenerationBound256Multibyte` |\n71|| 27 | Key material exact per engine row (4 literal derivations) | `TestKeySegmentsDerivesRowMaterial` |\n72|| 28 | Carried-key inconsistency refuses protocol, never mismatch | `TestCheckMutationContextKeyMaterial` |\n73|| 29 | Per-op params (bootstrap, quiescence, proof, timeouts, evidence) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n74|| 30 | Go-level generation bound (hand-built 257 refuses stale) | `TestCheckMutationContextGenerationBound` |\n75|\n76|### Operation and status bodies (items 2, 5) — `ParseOperationBody`, `ParseStatusBody`\n77|\n78|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n79|| --- | --- | --- |\n80|| 31 | Three closed bodies admitted with parsed members | `TestParseOperationBodyAdmitsRows` |\n81|| 32 | Body member arms (member sets, generations, proof, timeouts, evidence, key consistency) | `TestParseOperationBodyRefusals` |\n82|| 33 | Body scope gate (7 refused operations) | `TestParseOperationBodyScopeGate` |\n83|| 34 | Status exact-instance and session-scoped lookups admitted | `TestParseStatusBodyAdmitsBothScopes` |\n84|| 35 | Status null-pair rule (exactly one null refuses) | `TestParseStatusBodyNullPairRule` |\n85|| 36 | Status member arms incl. generation 0/256/257 | `TestParseStatusBodyMemberRefusals` |\n86|\n87|### Result identity (item 2) — `CheckResult`, `buildResult`\n88|\n89|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n90|| --- | --- | --- |\n91|| 37 | Engine result repeats every identity, before equals source | `TestCheckResultAdmitsEngineResult` |\n92|| 38 | Every repeated identity tamper refuses (generation → stale class) | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper` (8 subtests) |\n93|| 39 | Generation 256 admitted in result