tExecuteDeadlineNeverCancelsCommittedEffect` |\n111|| 52 | Per-row timeout vocabulary (wait quiesce_timeout, stop stop_timeout, quiesce terminal_backend_timeout) | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes` (3 subtests) |\n112|\n113|### Generation-safe evidence (item 4)\n114|\n115|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n116|| --- | --- | --- |\n117|| 53 | Bound in every owned surface (context, status, result bodies; 0/256/257; chars not bytes) | Rows 26, 36, 39 |\n118|| 54 | Entry + per-effect staleness refuse the landed stale class | Rows 43 (generation subtests), 49, 50 |\n119|| 55 | Bound verdict agrees with landed GenerationDigest on the boundary corpus | `TestGenerationBoundAgreesWithLandedDigest` |\n120|| 56 | Landed row codes admitted by landed CheckErrorAllowed (in-set + outside-set) | `TestRowCodesAreAdmittedByCheckErrorAllowed` |\n121|\n122|### Operation rows (item 5) — `Engine.ExecuteMutating`, `Engine.ExecuteStatus`\n123|\n124|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n125|| --- | --- | --- |\n126|| 57 | status same-state from all 8 states + unknown source; zero effects and receipts | `TestExecuteStatusAllSources` |\n127|| 58 | status adopts drifted state verbatim (no transition bookkeeping) | `TestExecuteStatusAdoptsReportedState` |\n128|| 59 | status non-match adopts proven absent | `TestExecuteStatusNonMatchAdoptsAbsent` |\n129|| 60 | status unknown never absent (coded, uncoded, outside-set code) | `TestExecuteStatusUnknownIsNeverAbsent` |\n130|| 61 | status report validation (lying match, non-canonical form, unsorted evidence, matched-tuple false form) | `TestExecuteStatusReportValidation`, `TestExecuteStatusMatchedTupleFalseFormRefuses` |\n131|| 62 | status provider conditional exactly when requested | `TestExecuteStatusProviderConditional` |\n132|| 63 | status session-scoped lookup adopts the reported instance | `TestExecuteStatusSessionScoped` |\n133|| 64 | quiesce from active and parked to quiescing with input_closed | `TestExecuteQuiesceSuccess` (2 subtests) |\n134|| 65 | Row refusal sets exact (quiesce timeout in/stop_timeout out; wait quiesce_timeout in/backend timeout out; stop stop_timeout in/quiesce_timeout out) | `TestExecuteBackendRowErrorSets` |\n135|| 66 | wait quiescing to quiescing with safe_boundary_observed | `TestExecuteWaitSuccess` |\n136|| 67 | wait capabilities (safe always; provider iff provider kind; provider-only still needs safe) | `TestExecuteWaitCapabilityConditionals` (4 subtests) |\n137|| 68 | stop quiescing to stopped, 3 effects in transition order, reported sorted | `TestExecuteStopSuccess` |\n138|| 69 | create receipt rule (interactive to active, headless to parked, headless conditional) | `TestExecuteCreateReceiptRule` |\n139|| 70 | Idempotent replay, changed-operation mismatch, uncertain retry requires status | `TestExecuteIdenticalRetryReplays`, `TestExecuteChangedOperationInWindowMismatches`, `TestExecuteUncertainRetryRequiresStatus` |\n140|| 71 | Real-SIGKILL crash seam: pending survives, no completion, uncertain retry, status recovery | `TestExecuteCrashChildSelfTerminates` |\n141|| 72 | Landed conferral wiring (empty admitted, all 4 rows) and engine scope gate (6 refused ops) | `TestExecuteEmptyAdmittedRefusesAtLandedGate` (4 subtests), `TestExecuteScopeGate` |\n142|\n143|## Mutant table\n144|\n145|`mutant_harness.py`: 53 rows, two full passes, 52 KILLED + the SURVIVED\n146|control, per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits both passes,\n147|production blobs byte-identical before/after. Every row is narrowing\n148|except `N-auth-epoch-high` (tightening: the weakening direction is\n149|equivalent because `environ` refuses 2^53 at the number layer, so no\n150|weakening past `MaxLeaseEpoch` is observable; the row proves the edge is\n151|exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it) and `C-control` (harmless\n152|SURVIVED control).\n153|\n154|| Row | Gate | Killer |\n155|| --- | --- | --- |\n156|| N-auth-epoch-low | Epoch bound min edge (admits 0) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n157|| N-auth-epoch-high | Epoch bound max edge (refuses Max; tightening, see above) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n158|| N-auth-kind | Kind vocabulary (admits admin) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationKindClosed` |\n159|| N-auth-kind-binding | Kind binding (control as create) | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/kind_mismatch` |\n160|| N-auth-expiry | Expiry edge (admits the instant) | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/expiry_edge_refuses` |\n161|| N-auth-lease-id | Lease identity comparison | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_identity_drift` |\n162|| N-auth-lease-epoch | Lease epoch comparison | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_epoch_drift` |\n163|| N-auth-extra-member | Closed member set | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n164|| N-auth-expiry-order | Strict expiry order | `TestParseAXAuthorizationStrictExpiry` |\n165|| N-disp-parse | Disposition vocabulary (admits retry) | `TestParseRetryDispositionClosed` |\n166|| N-disp-unauthorized | Mapping: committed unauthorized | `TestDispositionForMapping` |\n167|| N-disp-timeout | Mapping: uncommitted quiesce_timeout | `TestDispositionForMapping` |\n168|| N-disp-stop | Mapping: stop_timeout group membership | `TestDispositionForMapping` |\n169|| N-disp-default | Mapping: uncommitted capability default | `TestDispositionForMapping` |\n170|| N-proof-vocab | Proof vocabulary (admits provider_restart) | `TestParseProviderProofKindClosed` |\n171|| N-proof-provider | Provider classification (AX boundary) | `TestRequiresProviderObservation` |\n172|| N-context-key | Key material equality (same-length wrong keys) | `TestCheckMutationContextKeyMaterial` |\n173|| N-context-generation | Go-level generation bound (admits 257) | `TestCheckMutationContextGenerationBound` |\n174|| N-wait-timeout-bound | Timeout bound (admits 3600001) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n175|| N-body-key | Body key consistency (quiesce only) | `TestParseOperationBodyRefusals` |\n176|| N-result-operation | Repetition: operation (admits tampered ID) | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/operation` |\n177|| N-result-session | Repetition: session | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/session` |\n178|| N-result-instance | Repetition: instance | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/instance` |\n179|| N-result-backend | Repetition: backend | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/backend` |\n180|| N-result-implementation | Repetition: implementation | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/implementation` |\n181|| N-result-protocol | Repetition: protocol | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/protocol` |\n182|| N-result-generation | Repetition: generation | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/generation` |\n183|| N-result-before | Repetition: before state | `TestCheckResultRepetitionTamper/before` |\n184|| N-result-effects-order | Effects order half | `TestCheckResultShapeArms` |\n185|| N-result-evidence-unique | Evidence uniqueness half | `TestCheckResultShapeArms` |\n186|| N-store-mismatch-op | Mismatch: operation half | `TestStoreBindReplayMismatch` |\n187|| N-store-mismatch-id | Mismatch: operation-ID half | `TestStoreBindReplayMismatch` |\n188|| N-store-replay | Replay signal (fixture key) | `TestExecuteIdenticalRetryReplays` |\n189|| N-store-torn | Torn receipt (4-byte file as absence) | `TestStoreLookupAbsenceIsNotFailure` |\n190|| N-complete-unbound | Completion without receipt | `TestStoreCompleteRequiresReceipt` |\n191|| N-fencing-epoch-only | Fencing: lease-mismatch arm dropped | `TestObserveFencingLeaseMismatchFences` |\n192|| N-fencing-remote | Fencing: remote parks fenced | `TestObserveFencingNonStaleLeavesState` |\n193|| N-engine-checkoperation | CheckOperation wiring (wait only) | `TestExecuteEmptyAdmittedRefusesAtLandedGate/wait-safe-boundary` |\n194|| N-engine-transition | CheckTransition wiring (stopped sources) | `TestExecutePreEffectErrorsRestoreSource/illegal_source_refuses` |\n195|| N-engine-deadline-pre | Entry deadline (wait only; receipt bound) | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/wait-safe-boundary` |\n196|| N-engine-timeout-code | Row timeout code (wait reports stop code) | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/wait-safe-boundary` |\n197|| N-engine-auth-entry | Pre-bind auth gate (fixture op) | `TestExecutePreEffectErrorsRestoreSource/entry_auth_expired` |\n198|| N-engine-generation-entry | Pre-bind generation gate (fixture op) | `TestExecutePreEffectErrorsRestoreSource/entry_generation_stale` |\n199|| N-engine-recheck-auth | Per-effect auth recheck (pre-first skipped) | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeEachEffect/rotation_before_first_effect_restores_source` |\n200|| N-engine-recheck-generation | Per-effect generation recheck (pre-first skipped) | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeEachEffect/generation_rotation_before_first_effect_restores_source` |\n201|| N-engine-precommit-after | Pre-commit after-state (timeouts to unavailable) | `TestExecutePreEffectErrorsRestoreSource/coded_backend_refusal_on_first_effect` |\n202|| N-engine-postcommit-after | Post-commit after-state (process failures to source) | `TestExecutePostEffectErrorsMoveUnavailable/coded_refusal_on_second_effect` |\n203|| N-engine-status-match | Status match equality (absent-state lies) | `TestExecuteStatusMatchedTupleFalseFormRefuses` |\n204|| N-engine-status-unknown | Status unknown (uncoded reported absent) | `TestExecuteStatusUnknownIsNeverAbsent` |\n205|| N-engine-status-conditional | Status provider conditional (fixture backend) | `TestExecuteStatusProviderConditional` |\n206|| N-status-nullpair | Status null-pair rule (one half) | `TestParseStatusBodyNullPairRule` |\n207|| N-interim | Interim creating (quiesce too) | `TestExecuteInterimState` |\n208|| C-control | Comment-only control (SURVIVED) | `TestRequiresProviderObservation` |\n209|\n210|## Stated bounds\n211|\n212|- No `ax` command, no doctor result, no runtime capability claim: the\n213|  `Backend` interface is modeled; tmux/ConPTY/process control and the\n214|  provider process do not exist here.\n215|- Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed-object parsing: no parser\n216|  exists on trunk (`canonicaljson` explicitly rejects\n217|  `urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding`); the generation bound is\n218|  enforced on the surfaces this leaf owns and cited landed for the\n219|  Provider Protocol 3 descriptor (`terminalbackend` checkGeneration\n220|  arms). Full Binding parsing belongs with the provisioning surface.\n221|- CLI Result 4 summary: no landed Result 4 body carries a raw\n222|  generation member (`internal/cliresult` carries none by grep), so\n223|  there is no surface to witness the bound on; consistent with §4.E\n224|  (generation is host-local, non-replicable).\n225|- Attach, restore, terminate-stale, manifest, probe: refused by the\n226|  engine and body scope gates. Restore/terminate-stale recovery and\n227|  terminal binding events belong to the story's final leaf.\n228|- Create is receipt-scoped: receipt, transition, target and headless\n229|  rules execute; the full create body (Binding, Entrypoint,\n230|  presentation transport) belongs to provisioning.\n231|- Credential-realm conditional: credential need is not modeled on the\n232|  engine path.\n233|- Protocol_version membership in the admitted probe list is enforced at\n234|  registry admission (landed), not re-derived per operation; the\n235|  operation gate enforces grammar plus major 1 through the landed\n236|  `CheckVersionTuple` arms.\n237|- The per-code disposition mapping is the leaf's contract where the\n238|  spec pins the vocabulary but not the mapping; every arm is pinned\n239|  literally and mutated.\n240|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract; the final\n241|  leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin.\n242|\n243|## Inherited advisories (predecessor P3, for the record)\n244|\n245|- P3-6 closed by this leaf: the `Decision.Descriptor` doc in\n246|  `internal/axpane/decide.go` now states the recorded Binding\n247|  terminal instance ID is authoritative on reattach; this package's\n248|  `doc.go` states the consumer side.\n249|- P3-2 bound stated: this leaf adds no I/O-free `Decide` caller (the\n250|  engine never calls `Decide`), so the missing-closure input shape is\n251|  unreachable from this package; the pure-core hardening stays with\n252|  the owner.\n253|- P3-3 bound stated: this leaf never loads checkpoints (no\n254|  `LoadCheckpoint` caller), so the absent-store shape is unreachable\n255|  from this package.\n256|- P3-1, P3-4, P3-5 left to the final leaf (TASK-260830-2056mm):\n257|  journal-only restore closure (recovery domain), `EmitParked`\n258|  winner binding (events domain) and the corrupt-blob negative\n259|  (recovery domain) belong to events-and-recovery work.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
