{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc8d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":1185,"recorded_at":1780531400002365,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b23b-2970-79a2-9bff-c1feab7866da"},"task_id":"01a0b23b-2970-79a2-9bff-c1feab7866da","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b23b-2970-79a2-9bff-c1feab7866da","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(923 line(s) above)\n924|### 4.B Registry, identity, discovery, and trust\n925|\n926|<code>terminal_backend_id</code> is 1–128 ASCII bytes matching\n927|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*</code>. The <code>ax.</code> namespace is\n928|reserved. Canonical built-ins are <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n929|<code>ax.conpty</code>. Third parties use a stable vendor-owned namespace. No\n930|normative Superlogical ID is reserved.\n931|\n932|Terminal Backend Manifest 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no\n933|other member is permitted:\n934|\n935|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n936|| --- | --- |\n937|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> |\n938|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n939|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n940|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n941|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver |\n942|| <code>protocol_versions</code> | sorted unique semver[1..32], each in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n943|| <code>platforms</code> | sorted unique enum[1..4] from <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> |\n944|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | <code>builtin_go|local_program|trusted_executable|native_runtime</code> |\n945|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest for <code>local_program</code> or <code>trusted_executable</code>; null otherwise |\n946|| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\n947|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest |\n948|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code>; non-empty extensions require a later contract version |\n949|\n950|Terminal Backend Probe 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable observation; no\n951|other member is permitted:\n952|\n953|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n954|| --- | --- |\n955|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> |\n956|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n957|| <code>probe_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n958|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n959|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to the admitted Manifest |\n960|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver selected from the Manifest's <code>protocol_versions</code> |\n961|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | enum equal to the Manifest member |\n962|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest|null exactly equal to the Manifest member |\n963|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>, contained in the Manifest's <code>platforms</code> |\n964|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] |\n965|| <code>availability</code> | <code>available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code> |\n966|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest of the domain-separated raw generation |\n967|| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\n968|| <code>evidence_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..256] referencing Capability Evidence 1.0.0 |\n969|| <code>probed_at</code> | timestamp |\n970|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n971|\n972|The generation digest uses SHA-256 over UTF-8\n973|<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\\0</code> followed by the backend's\n974|host-local raw generation bytes; it neither reveals nor reconstructs that\n975|generation. Manifest-to-Probe reconciliation is the following closed rule. The\n976|Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,\n977|<code>implementation_kind</code>, and <code>executable_digest</code> MUST equal\n978|the Manifest members; its <code>protocol_version</code> MUST be exactly one member\n979|of <code>protocol_versions</code>, and its <code>platform</code> MUST be exactly\n980|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n981|not aggregate equality.\n982|\n983|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n984|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n985|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n986|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n987|\n988|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n989|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n990|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n991|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n992|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n993|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n994|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n995|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n996|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n997|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n998|   the capability registry row.\n999|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n1000|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n1001|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n1002|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n1003|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n1004|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n1005|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n1006|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n1007|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n1008|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n1009|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n1010|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n1011|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n1012|   literal <code>true</code>.\n1013|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n1014|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n1015|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n1016|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n1017|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n1018|\n1019|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n1020|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n1021|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n1022|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n1023|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n1024|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n1025|\n1026|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n1027|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n1028|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n1029|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n1030|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n1031|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n1032|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n1033|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n1034|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n1035|validate the boundary.\n1036|\n1037|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1038|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1039|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1040|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1041|\n1042|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1043|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1044|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1045|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1046|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1047|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1048|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1049|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1050|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1051|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1052|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1053|\n1054|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1055|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1056|permitted:\n1057|\n1058|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1059|| --- | --- |\n1060|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1061|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1062|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1063|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1064|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1065|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1066|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1067|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1068|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1069|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1070|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1071|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1072|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1073|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1074|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1075|\n1076|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1077|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1078|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1079|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1080|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1081|\n1082|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1083|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
