{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cccd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":1217,"recorded_at":1780531400002429,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b23b-6a92-76a0-be86-19c5c55f1834"},"task_id":"01a0b23b-6a92-76a0-be86-19c5c55f1834","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b23b-6a92-76a0-be86-19c5c55f1834","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(1219 line(s) above)\n1220|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1221|\n1222|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1223|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1224|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1225|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1226|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1227|\n1228|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1229|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1230|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1231|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1232|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1233|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1234|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1235|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1236|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1237|\n1238|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1239|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1240|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1241|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1242|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1243|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1244|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1245|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1246|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1247|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1248|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1249|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1250|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1251|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1252|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1253|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1254|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1255|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1256|\n1257|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1258|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1259|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1260|member is permitted:\n1261|\n1262|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1263|| --- | --- |\n1264|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1265|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1266|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1267|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1268|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1269|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1270|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1271|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1272|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1273|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1274|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1275|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1276|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1277|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1278|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1279|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1280|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1281|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1282|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1283|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1284|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1285|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1286|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1287|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1288|\n1289|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1290|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1291|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1292|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1293|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1294|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1295|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1296|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1297|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1298|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1299|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1300|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1301|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1302|change and before activation.\n1303|\n1304|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1305|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1306|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1307|activation when policy allows.\n1308|\n1309|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
