 TerminalBackendCapability |\n1272|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1273|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1274|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1275|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1276|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1277|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1278|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1279|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1280|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1281|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1282|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1283|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1284|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1285|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1286|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1287|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1288|\n1289|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1290|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1291|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1292|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1293|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1294|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1295|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1296|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1297|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1298|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1299|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1300|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1301|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1302|change and before activation.\n1303|\n1304|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1305|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1306|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1307|activation when policy allows.\n1308|\n1309|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
