ignatureVerifier verifies one evidence attestation signature. issuerID is\n1504|// the evidence issuer_id, message the domain-separated canonical bytes from\n1505|// UnsignedEvidenceBytes, and signature the decoded attestation bytes. A nil\n1506|// return authenticates through the caller's trusted release or\n1507|// host-incarnation key registry; any error (unknown key, invalid signature,\n1508|// registry failure) fails closed. A nil verifier admits nothing.\n1509|type SignatureVerifier func(issuerID string, message, signature []byte) error\n1510|\n1511|// integrityFailure refuses with CodeIntegrityFailure and a static detail.\n1512|//\n1513|//go:noinline\n1514|func integrityFailure(detail string) *Error {\n1515|\terr := &Error{Code: CodeIntegrityFailure, Detail: detail}\n1516|\tif recordRefusal != nil {\n1517|\t\trecordRefusal(err.Code, err.Detail)\n1518|\t}\n1519|\treturn err\n1520|}\n1521|\n1522|// UnsignedEvidenceBytes rebuilds the exact bytes an attestation signs: ASCII\n1523|// evidenceSignatureDomain, one zero byte, and the RFC 8785 JCS bytes of the\n1524|// evidence object with exactly evidence_id and attestation_signature\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
