{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e301","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b232-ed9f-73f2-b41b-df749face5b0"},"sequence":4059,"recorded_at":1780531400008113,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5f437c29-0343-41ba-a118-050af5991fa2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b262-4fe6-7e43-b627-4d20a30461fb"},"task_id":"01a0b262-4fe6-7e43-b627-4d20a30461fb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b262-4fe6-7e43-b627-4d20a30461fb","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 8-16\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\n-- DELIVERED: `internal/terminstance` — the §4.C execution layer over the landed `terminalbackend` core: closed `AXAuthorization` (UUIDv4 lease, uint53 epoch bound, UUIDv7 holder, kind, timestamps, digest) through the `environ` closed-shape discipline, closed `RetryDisposition`/`ProviderProofKind` enums, the `MutationContext`/`MutationResult` identity contract with exact per-row idempotency material, and the `Engine` (durable receipt before first effect, per-effect auth+generation rechecks, source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` post-commit, deadline cancels waiting never committed effects). `stale_fenced` enters only through `fencing` park vocabulary; status is receipt/effect-free and unknown is never absent. Second leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\n-- F1: quiesce-input and request-stop carry no conditional beyond conferral — their spec capabilities are their sole conferring registry rows — so the landed `CheckOperation` decides those rows alone and a second arm restating it would be dead code; the engine's conditional covers only create-headless, wait-safe-plus-provider-iff, and status-provider, where the spec demands more than conferral.\n-- F2: the receipt's no-replace commit needs a separate completion file, because the result is unknown at bind time and updating the receipt in place would break no-replace; pending-without-done is therefore the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` with `status_first` instead of replaying or inventing absence.\n-- F3: the epoch high edge cannot be weakened past `environ`'s own uint53 ceiling (same value, equivalent mutant), so that harness row tightens instead and proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it; the min edge, the delegate's ceiling, and the tightening row triangulate the bound.\n-- F4: closed P3-6 from the predecessor review (the `Decision.Descriptor` doc now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on reattach); P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader in this package); P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to the final leaf with the recovery/events reasons.\n-- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 51 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 53/53 with the harmless SURVIVED control), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n-- AC: 72 of 72 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`, every named test verified present via `go test -list`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-SIGKILL pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n-- F5 (finding, pre-existing): `TestSmokeThroughRealProviderProcess` (`internal/resumesmoke`, `probe=fail`) fails identically on the committed base HEAD without this leaf's changes and has no dependency edge to either leaf (`go list -deps` clean; base packages untouched by both leaves), so commands 4–6 report exit 1 with that single named cause while all 38 other packages — including `terminstance`, `axpane`, `terminalbackend` — are green in the full, race, and coverage runs alike.\n+### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/terminstance` — the §4.C execution layer over the landed `terminalbackend` core: closed `AXAuthorization` (UUIDv4 lease, uint53 epoch bound, UUIDv7 holder, kind, timestamps, digest) through the `environ` closed-shape discipline, closed `RetryDisposition`/`ProviderProofKind` enums, the `MutationContext`/`MutationResult` identity contract with exact per-row idempotency material, and the `Engine` (durable receipt before first effect, per-effect auth+generation rechecks, source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` post-commit, deadline cancels waiting never committed effects). `stale_fenced` enters only through `fencing` park vocabulary; status is receipt/effect-free and unknown is never absent. Second leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\n+- REFRESH: rev1 was constructed on `e6fe5c5` and its suite stopped at command 4/30 on the trunk resumesmoke time bomb (fixed as `a12d1bd`); this run refreshed the candidate onto `c3aae73` (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay, 29 stale trunk-changed paths restored to the new HEAD, LOGBOOK/README/decide.go rebased purely additive, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical), inherited the rev1 worktree delta verbatim, and re-verified it against SPEC.v0.7.0 plus the landed owners instead of redoing it.\n+- F1: quiesce-input and request-stop carry no conditional beyond conferral — their spec capabilities are their sole conferring registry rows — so the landed `CheckOperation` decides those rows alone and a second arm restating it would be dead code; the engine's conditional covers only create-headless, wait-safe-plus-provider-iff, and status-provider, where the spec demands more than conferral.\n+- F2: the receipt's no-replace commit needs a separate completion file, because the result is unknown at bind time and updating the receipt in place would break no-replace; pending-without-done is therefore the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` with `status_first` instead of replaying or inventing absence.\n+- F3: the epoch high edge cannot be weakened past `environ`'s own uint53 ceiling (same value, equivalent mutant), so that harness row tightens instead and proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it; the min edge, the delegate's ceiling, and the tightening row triangulate the bound.\n+- F4: closed P3-6 from the predecessor review (the `Decision.Descriptor` doc now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on reattach); P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader in this package); P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to the final leaf with the recovery/events reasons.\n+- F5 (this run): the staging sweep deleted every `*.tmp` unconditionally, so a concurrent `Bind` could lose its live stage and fail its link spuriously — now age-gated (1 min, crash garbage ages out, readers ignore staging names), pinned by keep/sweep tests plus a narrowing row. Also closed this run: the `doc.go` drift claim (§13.1 carries the v0.7.0 launch-plan pure-addition insertion, so \"byte-identical in scope\" was false — reworded precisely), the missing create entry-deadline and first-effect reported-`stop_timeout` pins (the two stop directions now measured together), the unmeasured kind-mapping/fencing-operation/timeout-code/status-source gates (new rows), the six `checkParams` arms (new rows; the bootstrap row caught a weak `err==nil` assertion, now literal), the Go-level version arms, the malformed-reported-member status arms, and the wire-order sorts (new rows).\n+- F6 (bounds stated, not built): AX-side seam verdicts (uncoded effect → `terminal_backend_process_failed`, uncertain retry → `terminal_backend_unavailable`) sit outside the §4.C row sets, which govern backend reports via `CheckErrorAllowed`; the wait/stop lesser-of-timeout is enforced by the backend wait (validated and carried in `Params`, engine enforces `deadline_at`); document member weakenings masked by a same-detail Go twin carry their narrowing row on the twin.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 68 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 70/70 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n+- AC: 72 of 72 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`; 70 named top-level tests all present via `go test -list`, 7 cited subtests all `--- PASS`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-SIGKILL pattern. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded chunks with identical flags, 40/40 packages, no DATA RACE; tracecheck `56/569` trunk figures unchanged). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n","final_result":true}}}
